<!--
    Default locale = ARABIC (ANSWERS.md §12). English lives in values-en/.

    A3 classified provider failures, resolved by AiError.toUserMessage() in
    com.braining.core.ui.error. They live in core-ui rather than in a feature module because
    both feature-chat and feature-settings phrase them and both already depend on core-ui —
    see the KDoc on AiErrorMessage.kt and PROJECT_STATE.md §10 entry 2026-08-04-B.

    The prefix is `error_` rather than `chat_`: library resources merge into one app-wide
    namespace, so the name must be unique but must no longer claim to belong to chat.

    Every message names the provider. The HTTP status appears only where the error carries
    one — missing key, no network and timeout have no status because nothing was ever sent.
    RegionBlocked deliberately shows no code: the ruling (ANSWERS.md Part 3 §B) is to state
    the refusal in plain Arabic and steer the user to another provider.
-->
