    <!--
        M5.1 · THE APP'S NAME — one place, two locales.

        The owner's ruling of 2026-08-28: **«فهم» in Arabic, «Braining» in English.** «مِداد» is
        the name of the visual identity and is deliberately NOT shown to the user; it belongs to
        `docs/BRAND.md`, not to a screen.

        **It lives here, in `:core-ui`, and not in the app module.** The launcher label could read
        it from anywhere, but the first-run flow greets the user by the app's name — and a library
        module cannot see the app module's `R` (§10 entry 18). Every screen depends on `:core-ui`,
        so this is the one place all of them can read.

        **Never hardcode the name in Kotlin or in another string.** It changes with the device's
        language, and a copy would freeze one of the two.
    -->
    <string name="app_name">فهم</string>

